.git
.claude
# What a Dockerfile `COPY . .` must never carry into a layer (p6-ops): the secret files (the root directory and any directory of the
# name below the tree), the signed node bundles, every copy of the host's .env that the scripts write beside it (.env.bak*,
# .env.prev, .env.new.*, the domain-apply lock) and the NTS keys of chrony. Most are gitignored, but deploy/bundles holds a tracked
# README.md and the chrony directory has no rule, so no review would see one in a layer. deploy/compose/.env.example stays: the Go
# image embeds the compose file beside it. internal/lint TestDockerignoreKeepsSecretsAndBundlesOutOfTheContext holds these lines.
secrets
**/secrets
deploy/bundles
deploy/compose/.env*
!deploy/compose/.env.example
deploy/chrony/nts
**/node_modules
**/.next
*.exe
*.test
*.out
deploy/compose/.env
docs
.codegraph
apps
packages
content
tools/web-lint
pnpm-lock.yaml
pnpm-workspace.yaml
package.json
tsconfig.base.json
eslint.config.mjs
.npmrc
